{"text": "OFFICE OF THE GOVERNOR\nJanuary 22, 2020\n\nVia Electronic Mail\n\nChava Gourarie\n85371-16705980@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRE: Public Records Act Request\n\nDear Ms. Gourarie;\n\nThis letter is in response to your correspondence received January 13, 2020, requesting,\n\u201cAll emails and correspondence between Governor Gavin Newsom or members of his staff AND\nTim Cook, CEO of Apple; or other employees of Apple; or employees of Facebook, sent or\nreceived between January 1, 2019 and the date of receipt of this request [January 13, 2020].\u201d\n\nAlthough we have identified records responsive to your request, those records are exempt\nfrom disclosure under the Public Records Act. In particular, those records are exempt from\ndisclosure because they are records of correspondence of or to the Governor\u2019s staff (Gov. Code,\n\u00a7 6254, subd. (J); and because they reveal the deliberative processes of the Governor and his\nAdministration (Gov. Code, \u00a7 6255; Times Mirror Co. v. Superior Court (1991) 53 Cal.3d 1325).\n\nAlso, please be advised that we are not the custodian of records from the Brown\nAdministration. You may wish to contact the California State Archives:\n\n1020 O Street\nSacramento, CA 95814\n(916) 653-7715\n\nThank you for contacting Governor Newsom\u2019s office.\n\nSincerely,\n\nZ WwW \u201c(2\u2014\nDAVID SAPP\nDeputy Legal Affairs Secretary\n\nGOVERNOR GAVIN NEWSOM \u00ab SACRAMENTO, CA 95814 * (916) 445-2841",
"words": [
